data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the template with `@typeparam TItem`, renders each item via `ItemTemplate`, and provides Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:
- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` swap elements in the internal copy and invoke `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only snapshot.

Usage matches your example:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [ /* ... */ ];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
